meta {
  name: UpdateProject — it links the board
  type: grpc
  seq: 4
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.HierarchyService/UpdateProject
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "project": {
        "id": "{{projectId}}",
        "workspace": { "id": "{{workspaceId}}" },
        "name": "Cockpit",
        "description": "An example project",
        "task_manager": {
          "integration": { "id": "{{integrationId}}" },
          "external_space_id": "sp-901",
          "external_project_id": "pj-42",
          "card_types": ["bug", "feature"]
        },
        "rules": ["no-green-no-pr"]
      }
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5).

  `external_space_id` is the **provider's space**, never our word "workspace":
  both concepts exist and confusing them is the short path to linking the project
  to the wrong board.

  `card_types` comes from the provider and is dynamic — the platform imposes no
  card vocabulary (ADR-0013).

  An update is a replacement: sending a null `task_manager` UNLINKS the board.
  Sending the project without the fields you do not want to lose erases what was
  there.
}
